- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/combinenormals.html
- Summary (EN): Combine Normals merges two normal maps into one. The base map carries the larger-scale detail and the detail map adds fine surface detail. For layers that are not normal maps, the page points to the Blend COP instead.
- Résumé (FR) : Le nœud Combine Normals fusionne deux cartes de normales, la base portant le détail large et la carte de détail ajoutant le relief fin, selon la méthode Whiteout, UDN ou Reoriented.

- Inputs meaning: ["bg: base normal map (background layer)", "fg: detail normal map (foreground blend source)", "mask (optional): per-pixel mask scaled by the Mask parameter"]

- Key parameters: ["Mask: how much of the new value is mixed in, default 1", "Normal Type: Signed (-1 to 1, e.g. geometry normals) or Offset (0 to 1, e.g. normal map textures); output matches", "Combine Method: Whiteout (adds x and y, multiplies z), UDN (adds x and y, keeps base z, faster), Reoriented (rotates detail onto base, more accurate, slower)"]

- Caveats: ["Both inputs must be in the same space (e.g. tangent) and the same type (both signed or both offset)", "Use the Convert Normal COP first to convert mismatched inputs"]

